  </table:table><text:p text:style-name="ToPortrait">Discussion</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Each volunteer described the condition of the wooden pier over three consecutive weeks. The lighthouse crew described the growth of moss on the old stone walls over three consecutive weeks. The fictional cooperative measured the amount of rain collected in copper gauges for the annual report. A small working group mapped the amount of rain collected in copper gauges using only paper notebooks. The lighthouse crew mapped the amount of rain collected in copper gauges over three consecutive weeks. A small working group reviewed the routes taken by the ferry during storms for the annual report.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The fictional cooperative summarised the songs sung at the autumn market over three consecutive weeks. The fictional cooperative compared the height of the hedges along the canal before the season ended. The archive keeper recorded the tidal patterns of the northern bay with remarkable patience. A small working group recorded the condition of the wooden pier despite the persistent fog. The archive keeper mapped the weight of the fishing nets after each trip using only paper notebooks.</text:p></office:text></office:body>
</office:document>
